  "security_implications": "JTAG-visible boot status (clock, OTP/LC done, halt FSM, CPU fetch enable, greenlight) is gated solely on lc_dft_en_i. If DFT mode is accidentally enabled or the guard bypassed, sensitive boot progression details leak to JTAG, aiding reverse engineering or fault injection. Greenlight signals use mubi4 integrity checks, but access control relies entirely on lc_dft_en_i, missing explicit lifecycle state checks.",
